        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_encrypt</definition>
        <argsstring>(const uint32_t key[4U], const uint32_t nonce[4U], uint8_t *plaintext, uint32_t plaintext_size, const uint8_t *associated_data, uint32_t associated_size, uint32_t authentication_tag[4U])</argsstring>
        <name>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_encrypt</name>
        <param>
          <type>const uint32_t</type>
          <declname>key</declname>
          <array>[4U]</array>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint32_t</type>
          <declname>nonce</declname>
          <array>[4U]</array>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>plaintext</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>plaintext_size</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>const uint8_t *</type>
          <declname>associated_data</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>associated_size</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>uint32_t</type>
          <declname>authentication_tag</declname>
          <array>[4U]</array>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Ascon-AEAD128 authenticated encryption. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Encrypts <computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> in place and produces a 128-bit authentication tag over the ciphertext and, when <computeroutput>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF</computeroutput> is defined, over <computeroutput>associated_data</computeroutput> as well. The operation follows Algorithm 3 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 4.1.1.</para>
<para>On return, the buffer addressed by <computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> holds the ciphertext of equal length. The original plaintext is overwritten and cannot be recovered from <computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> alone.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">key</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>128-bit secret key. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">nonce</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>128-bit public nonce. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">plaintext</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>On entry: plaintext buffer of <computeroutput>plaintext_size</computeroutput> bytes. On return: ciphertext of equal length, written in place. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">plaintext_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Length of <computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> in bytes. May be zero, in which case no plaintext blocks are processed and the tag covers only associated data.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">associated_data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to associated data of <computeroutput>associated_size</computeroutput> bytes. Authenticated but not encrypted. Only present when <computeroutput>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF</computeroutput> is defined. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">associated_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Length of <computeroutput>associated_data</computeroutput> in bytes. May be zero. Only present when <computeroutput>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF</computeroutput> is defined.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="out">authentication_tag</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>128-bit authentication tag produced after finalisation, written as four consecutive 32-bit words.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>key</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>nonce</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>authentication_tag</computeroutput> are non-NULL. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> points to a buffer of at least <computeroutput>plaintext_size</computeroutput> bytes. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>plaintext</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>authentication_tag</computeroutput> do not overlap. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para>The nonce is used at most once for a given key. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
