        <briefdescription>
<para>Ascon-AEAD128 authenticated decryption. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Decrypts <computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> in place and verifies the 128-bit authentication tag over the plaintext and, when <computeroutput>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF</computeroutput> is defined, over <computeroutput>associated_data</computeroutput> as well. The operation follows Algorithm 4 of NIST SP 800-232 Section 4.1.1.</para>
<para>On return, the buffer addressed by <computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> holds the plaintext of equal length. The original ciphertext is overwritten and cannot be recovered from <computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> alone.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">key</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>128-bit secret key. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">nonce</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>128-bit public nonce. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="inout">ciphertext</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>On entry: ciphertext buffer of <computeroutput>ciphertext_size</computeroutput> bytes. On return: plaintext of equal length, written in place. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">ciphertext_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Length of <computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> in bytes. May be zero, in which case no ciphertext blocks are processed and the tag covers only associated data.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">associated_data</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to associated data of <computeroutput>associated_size</computeroutput> bytes. Authenticated but not decrypted. Only present when <computeroutput>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF</computeroutput> is defined. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">associated_size</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Length of <computeroutput>associated_data</computeroutput> in bytes. May be zero. Only present when <computeroutput>VERUM_ASCON_AEAD128_ASSOCIATED_DATA_DEF</computeroutput> is defined.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">authentication_tag</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>128-bit authentication tag to verify after finalisation, read as four consecutive 32-bit words.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>key</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>nonce</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>authentication_tag</computeroutput> are non-NULL. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> points to a buffer of at least <computeroutput>ciphertext_size</computeroutput> bytes. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para><computeroutput>ciphertext</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>authentication_tag</computeroutput> do not overlap. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="pre"><para>The nonce matches the one used during encryption. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
