    <briefdescription>
<para>Ascon-AEAD128 authenticated encryption. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Authenticated Encryption with Associated Data (AEAD) is a form of encryption that simultaneously guarantees confidentiality of the plaintext and authenticity of both the plaintext and the associated data. Associated data is authenticated but not encrypted, it is tamper-evident. ASCON-AEAD128 realises this construction through a duplex sponge operating over a 320-bit permutation state, binding a 128-bit key and a 128-bit nonce to produce a ciphertext equal in length to the plaintext and a 128-bit authentication tag, as standardised in NIST SP 800-232.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ulink url="https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-232">https://doi.org/10.6028/NIST.SP.800-232</ulink></para>
</simplesect>
